#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:251
msgid "No. Frames (Test):"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:257
msgid ""
"Number of video frames to process in the diagnostic test.\n"
"Use a low value (e.g. 100) for quick tests."
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:266
msgid "Confidence Threshold:"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:272
msgid ""
"Confidence Threshold\n"
"\n"
"Minimum probability (0.0 to 1.0) for a detection to count as valid.\n"
"• Raise it (e.g. 0.50) if there are many 'false positives' "
"(noise/ghosts).\n"
"• Lower it (e.g. 0.15) if the fish is not detected in some frames.\n"
"• Recommended default: 0.25"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:283
msgid "NMS Threshold:"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:289
msgid ""
"NMS Threshold (Non-Maximum Suppression)\n"
"\n"
"Controls the removal of duplicate boxes for the same object.\n"
"• Low values (e.g. 0.4) merge overlapping boxes aggressively.\n"
"• High values (e.g. 0.7) allow more overlap.\n"
"• Recommended default: 0.50"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:304
msgid "Use ByteTrack (Advanced Tracking)"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:333
msgid "Track Thresh:"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:339
msgid ""
"Track Threshold (Tracking)\n"
"\n"
"Minimum confidence to START or KEEP a track.\n"
"• Defines how 'sure' the detector must be to create a new ID.\n"
"• Raise it to avoid junk/noise tracks.\n"
"• Lower it to keep the ID of fish that are hard to detect.\n"
"• Recommended default: 0.25"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:350
msgid "Match Thresh:"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:356
msgid ""
"Match Threshold\n"
"\n"
"Tolerance for associating a new detection with an existing track.\n"
"• High values (e.g. 0.8+) are more permissive (good for fast movement).\n"
"• Low values (<0.5) are restrictive (avoids identity swaps, but may lose "
"the track).\n"
"• Recommended default: 0.95"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:368
msgid "Track Buffer:"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:374
msgid ""
"Track Buffer (Memory)\n"
"\n"
"How many frames the system 'remembers' a fish after it disappears "
"(occlusion/miss).\n"
"• Raise it (e.g. 120) if the fish vanishes for a long time.\n"
"• Lower it to drop lost tracks quickly.\n"
"• Default: 90 frames (~3s at 30fps)"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:385
msgid "Max Dist. (px):"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:391
msgid ""
"Maximum Distance (pixels)\n"
"\n"
"How far the centre of the fish may move between processed frames.\n"
"• Prevents impossible associations (teleporting).\n"
"• Raise it if the fish is fast or the frame rate is low.\n"
"• Lower it if IDs are swapped between distant fish.\n"
"• Default: 400.0 px"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:403
msgid "IoU Thresh:"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:409
msgid ""
"IoU Threshold (Tracking)\n"
"\n"
"Minimum overlap (Intersection over Union) to associate boxes.\n"
"• Default: 0.05 (undemanding).\n"
"• Raise it (e.g. 0.3) to require the fish to stay in almost the same "
"position.\n"
"• Lower it to allow abrupt movements that change the box area."
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:422
msgid "Model(s) to Test:"
msgstr ""

#: src/zebtrack/ui/components/model_diagnostics_panel.py:458
msgid ""
"ℹ️ ByteTrack disabled. Using simple (Hybrid) tracking, which relies only "
"on 'Maximum Distance' and 'IoU Threshold' to keep the ID."
